-- title:
--   Theorem 2 — matroids: interaction is useless iff every component is a loop, a coloop, $U_{1,m}$ or $U_{m-1,m}$, iff no $U_{2,4}$ or $T$ minor
-- statement:
--   Fix $1<a<\infty$ and a finite matroid $\mathsf M$ on the users $E=\{1,\dots,n\}$, whose independent sets are the feasible sets. Then the following are equivalent:
--
--   1. interaction is useless for $\mathsf M$, that is, $W^{\mathrm I}=W^{\mathrm N}$ for every product prior and every arrival order;
--   2. every connected component $C$ of $\mathsf M$, with $m=|C|$, is a loop, a coloop, $U_{1,m}$ or $U_{m-1,m}$;
--   3. $\mathsf M$ has no minor isomorphic to $U_{2,4}$ or to $T$, the rank-two matroid on four elements whose parallel classes have sizes $2,1,1$.
--
--   This is the matroid specialization of the classification theorem: among matroids, a fixed randomizer per user is optimal for every prior and every order exactly when every component is a single rank-one or corank-one uniform matroid.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $U_{2,4}$ and $T$ are the published obstructions $O_7$ and $O_5$ (Lean `O 6` and `O 4`). A minor up to isomorphism is the published family minor: contraction of an independent set, then deletion, with an injective relabelling.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a finite matroid M → M : Matroid (Fin n) with ground set all of Fin n; feasible sets = indepFam M; reason: the users are Fin n in arrival order
--   - encoding: every connected component is a loop, a coloop, U_{1,m} or U_{m−1,m} → for every element u, with C = comp (indepFam M) u and m = |C|: C has size 1 and rank 0, or size 1 and rank 1, or the restriction to C is uniform of rank 1, or uniform of rank m − 1; reason: connected components are the classes generated by common circuits (the minimally infeasible sets); a restriction isomorphic to a uniform matroid on its own ground set is exactly a uniform restriction
--   - encoding: M has no minor isomorphic to U_{2,4} or to T → ¬ IsMinorOf (O 6) (indepFam M) ∧ ¬ IsMinorOf (O 4) (indepFam M); reason: every matroid minor is M/I∖D with I independent (§3.4, p.8); O 6 has circuits all 3-sets (U_{2,4}); O 4 has circuits 123, 124, 34 (rank two, parallel classes 2,1,1)
--   - encoding: interaction is useless → the published Useless: W^I = W^N for every arrival order σ and every integrable product prior; reason: the definition of §1.1, p.1
--   - encoding: every product prior → every family of probability measures on ℝ≥0 with finite means, indexed by arrival position; reason: the standing assumption of §2: values are independent, non-negative and integrable
--   - encoding: W^I and W^N of Definition 8 → the published WI and WN (suprema in [0, ∞] over output types Z : Type and private mechanisms with behaviour-strategy acceptance kernels); reason: the published base model of this mission, whose conventions are listed with LDPSelect.theorem_1
-- source:
--   Chen, Wang, When Does Private Data Collection Need Interaction? Online Selection under Local Differential Privacy, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 2e2d6157…), Theorem 2, p.2 (pdf p.3)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LDPSelect_Values
import Definitions.Def_LDPSelect_InClass
import Definitions.Def_LDPSelect_IsMinorOf
import Definitions.Def_LDPSelect_Obstructions
import Definitions.Def_LDPSelect_Supplement_Matroid

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory
open scoped NNReal ENNReal

namespace LDPSelect.Supplement

open LDPSelect

/-- Chen, Wang, *When Does Private Data Collection Need Interaction? Online Selection under Local Differential Privacy*, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 2e2d6157…), Theorem 2, p.2 (pdf p.3).

Fix `1 < a < ∞` and a finite matroid `M`. Interaction is useless for `M` if and only if every connected
component of `M` is a loop, a coloop, `U_{1,m}` or `U_{m−1,m}`, equivalently, if and only if `M` has no
minor isomorphic to `U_{2,4}` or to `T`, the rank-two matroid on four elements whose parallel classes
have sizes `2, 1, 1`.

**Formalization Note.** The matroid has ground set `Fin n` (`M.E = Set.univ`) and its feasible sets are
its independent sets. Components are the classes of the published `comp` (circuits are the minimally
infeasible sets); `m` is the size of the component. A minor up to isomorphism is the published
`IsMinorOf` (one contraction of an independent set, one deletion, an injective relabelling).
`O 6` is `U_{2,4}` and `O 4` (the paper's `O5`, circuits `123, 124, 34`) is `T`. "Interaction is useless"
is the published `Useless`: every arrival order and every integrable product prior. -/
theorem theorem_2 (a : ℝ) (ha : 1 < a) (n : ℕ) (M : Matroid (Fin n)) (hE : M.E = Set.univ) :
    (Useless a (indepFam M) ↔ IsLoopColoopUnifComps (indepFam M)) ∧
    (IsLoopColoopUnifComps (indepFam M) ↔
      ¬ IsMinorOf (O 6) (indepFam M) ∧ ¬ IsMinorOf (O 4) (indepFam M)) := by sorry

end LDPSelect.Supplement
